  "testId": "testClasses.webstore.quickOrder.QuickOrderPasteMultipleSKUsForGuestUserTest#pasteMultipleSkusForGuestUserVerifyInvalidSKUsAreNotAdding",
  "scenario": {
    "summary": "pastes two non-existent SKUs into the Add Multiple Items box and checks the '2 SKUs couldn't be added' message.",
    "steps": [
      "Open the webstore",
      "Quick Order, Add Multiple Items, Paste Multiple",
      "Clear the box; paste '<invalidSku1>, <defaultQuantity>' and '<invalidSku2>, <defaultQuantity>'; click Add All to Quick List",
      "Verify the message box text"
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "store"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [
      "None"
    ],
    "assertions": [
      "Message box text equals invalidProductValidationMessage"
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "invalidSku1 z-123564 / invalidSku2 z-123565 -> config: non-existent SKUs the test only needs to be invalid (Playwright profile: both NOT_FOUND). As the approved Playwright entry 'pasting invalid SKUs is rejected', they stay config values read from the sheet (coordinator decision 2026-11-05: no generated values). Nothing to resolve.",
      "defaultQuantity 0 is config; the message is expected-output (the count '2' is the point of the test).",
      "Store: openWebstoreUrl opens automation_webStoreUrl (atstage: webstore-z10-atstage, the main store MaxwellsHardware), the same store as the Selenium shoppingCart entries and the Playwright quick-order entries.",
      "Scanned constant values (locators, report messages, delays) are framework constants: role config, no need.",
      "migrate: Selenium reads Excel tables through TestData.getMap; there is no swap for Selenium."
    ],
    "confidence": "medium",
    "needsReview": true
  },
